  "raw": {
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/flexible_administrative_support_opportunity_at_the_stockholm_school_of_economics_hourly_up_to_20_-978776.html": {
      "title": "Flexible administrative support opportunity",
      "description": "Flexible administrative support opportunity at the Stockholm School of Economics (Hourly, up to 20%) Available Positions Departments Back Flexible administrative support opportunity at the Stockholm School of Economics (Hourly, up to 20%) Education Office The Education Office (EdO) is one of SSE’s Professional Services units and consists of around 58 colleagues. As a central part of the SSE journey, we support and develop key academic services for students and stakeholders across our BSc, MSc, and PhD programs. Our work spans assessment, program management, scholarships, international collaborations, academic support, central course and exam coordination, as well as degrees and certificates. Would you like to work in a dynamic international environment and contribute to the day-to-day operations of one of Europe's leading business schools? The Education Office at the Stockholm School of Economics (SSE) is building a small pool of flexible hourly staff who can provide support during peak periods and special projects throughout the year. As part of our support pool, you will step in where extra resources are needed most. Assignments vary over time and may involve administrative support related to admissions, student exchange, student services, events, information services, communication, and other Education Office activities. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys variety, is highly reliable, and can quickly adapt to new tasks and teams. Examples of assignments You may be asked to: Provide administrative support during admissions periods Assist with exchange and international mobility activities Support the Info Center and student-facing services Help coordinate events, welcome activities, and visits Assist with data entry, reporting, and quality assurance Support communication and information updates Contribute to project-based administrative tasks across the Education Office We are looking for someone who is Structured, accurate, and detail-oriented Service-minded and professional in interactions with students, faculty, staff, and visitors Flexible and comfortable handling different types of assignments Reliable and able to work independently Comfortable working in digital systems and administrative processes Fluent in English, both spoken and written Able to communicate in Swedish, as some assignments require interaction with Swedish-speaking stakeholders and documentation Comfortable handling information with discretion and confidentiality We offer A flexible hourly position with varied assignments Experience from multiple areas of higher education administration The opportunity to work with colleagues across the Education Office A welcoming and international work environment Flexible scheduling based on operational needs and your availability Hours: Approximately 4-8 hours per week (up to 20%) Location: Stockholm School of Economics, Stockholm Hourly salary: SEK 165/hour Start date : As soon as possible About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time First day of employment According to agreement Salary Hourly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent Hourly City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/72 Contact Ellen Falkenström Anna Dozai Ahlqvist Published 12.Oct.2026 Last application date 26.Oct.2026 11:59 PM CET Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/affiliated_researcher_position_in_the_project_solving_the_integration_challenge_of_high_skilled_migrants_the_central_role_of_merits__at_the_stockholm_school_of_economics_institute_for_research-975659.html": {
      "title": "Affiliated Researcher position in the project ‘Solving the integration challenge of high-skilled migrants: the central role of merits’",
      "description": "Affiliated Researcher position in the project ‘Solving the integration challenge of high-skilled migrants: the central role of merits’ – at the Stockholm School of Economics Institute for Research Available Positions Departments Back Affiliated Researcher position in the project ‘Solving the integration challenge of high-skilled migrants: the central role of merits’ – at the Stockholm School of Economics Institute for Research SIR About the position As an affiliated researcher joining an existing project, you will be expected to independently and together with the other researchers in the project contribute to: Conducting the analysis of a unique, large-scale recruitment database from a major Nordic company, containing applicant-level information across different positions Mapping and relating to current research on recruitment, discrimination, and labor market inclusion in Sociology and Management studies Conducting the analysis of the data from our survey experiments from a nationally representative sample using the Swedish Citizen Panel. The experiments investigate perceived integration merits of immigrants in Sweden Publishing original research on the basis of the recruitment database and the survey experiment Being part of the Center for Migration and Integration Research -CMIR is optional. If you wish to be part of CMIR, you will be expected to participate in the Center’s research activities (e.g. research seminars) and multistakeholder activities (e.g., workshops, roundtables, and dialogue forums) Your profile The successful candidate will have built a research agenda during their PhD, as evidenced by publications or conference papers, in the broad field of migration and integration. Their general disciplinary background should be within the social sciences, preferably in sociology or management with a focus on migration and integration. They master quantitative methods and have a very good understanding of survey experiments. Candidates should thrive in a collaborative environment while driving their contribution to the project independently. The applicants must hold a PhD by time of employment. They have shown ability and ambition to publish manuscripts in highly ranked, international scholarly journals.  We expect the candidate to relocate to Stockholm and to be physically present in the office. How to apply: Formal submission will be via the SSE Varbi online platform by latest November 1st, 2026. The following documents should be included in your application: A curriculum vitae A separate document listing published articles (if any) and articles submitted to journals, as well as other academic peer-reviewed publications (e.g., book chapters, conference proceedings). Copies of representative research, that is, copies of your publications or work in progress (max 5) Names and contact information for three people willing to provide references. We recommend that you apply as soon as possible and at the latest before November 1st, 2026. Starting date is flexible but preferably around December 2026. The employment is up to the end of December 2027. For further questions on the position, please contact Laurence Romani: laurence.romani@hhs.se or Andrea Voyer: Andrea.voyer@sociology.su.se The position is formally at the Stockholm School of Economics Institute for Research About Stockholm School of Economics Institute for Research Stockholm School of Economics Institute for Research is an independent research foundation, founded in 2010. The overall aim is to conduct qualified academic research within the economic sciences, which aims to unite scientific stringency with empirical relevance. The purpose of the Institute’s publications is to disseminate research concerning corporate enterprises and society. About the Center for Migration and Integration Research The Center for Migration and Integration Research (CMIR), housed at the SSE House of Governance and Public Policy (GaPP), aims to create a platform to support the sustainable integration of third-country nationals in Sweden. Together with key stakeholders in the migration and integration process, experiences and insights are researched and incorporated into a systemic perspective. The Center emphasizes the importance of the collaboration of multiple stakeholders in the governance of migration and integration, at multiple levels, and focuses not only on employment, but also on other dimensions of sustainable migration and integration. The research team collects, creates, and disseminates multiple-actor, science-based knowledge on the governance of migration and integration in Sweden for societal and social sustainability. Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time First day of employment Flexible, but preferably around December 2026 Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/69 Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 11:59 PM CET Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/two_tenure_track_positions_in_economics_to_the_stockholm_school_of_economics-974428.html": {
      "title": "Two tenure track positions in Economics to the Stockholm School of Economics",
      "description": "Two tenure track positions in Economics to the Stockholm School of Economics Available Positions Departments Back Two tenure track positions in Economics to the Stockholm School of Economics Department of Economics The Department of Economics at the Stockholm School of Economics (SSE) seeks candidates for two tenure-track assistant professor positions. Applicants from any field within economics will be considered (with particular focus on theory, microeconomics and applied microeconomics). The appointments start August 1, 2027, and applicants are expected to have completed their Ph.D. or equivalent degree by then. The deadline for applications is November 16, 2026. Applications should be submitted on the EconJobMarket.org website and should include a cover letter, CV, three letters of reference, and a job market paper (clearly labeled) as well as additional papers (optional). Interviews will be conducted online. We intend to interview most applicants in December 2026 around the time of the European Job Market. For further information about the Department of Economics, see https://www.hhs.se/research/departments/economics/ or contact petya.thorne@hhs.se. Interviews will be conducted remotely by video starting December 2026. To apply for this position, log in to your account at EconJobMarket. About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment 2027-08-01 Salary According to agreement Number of positions 2 Full-time equivalent 100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/66 Contact Petya Thorne Emma Hellsten Published 29.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Nov.2026 11:59 PM CET Share links A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/post_doc_position_at_the_center_for_migration_and_integration_at_the_stockholm_school_of_economics_sse__-973026.html": {
      "title": "Post-doc position",
      "description": "Post-doc position at the Center for Migration and Integration at the Stockholm School of Economics (SSE) Available Positions Departments Back Post-doc position at the Center for Migration and Integration at the Stockholm School of Economics (SSE) House of Governance and Public Policy (GaPP) About the Center for Migration and Integration Research The Center for Migration and Integration Research (CMIR), housed at the SSE House of Governance and Public Policy (GaPP), aims to create a platform to support the sustainable integration of third-country nationals in Sweden. Together with key stakeholders in the migration and integration process, experiences and insights are researched and incorporated into a systemic perspective. The Center emphasizes the importance of the collaboration of multiple stakeholders in the governance of migration and integration, at multiple levels, and focuses not only on employment, but also on other dimensions of sustainable migration and integration. The research team collects, creates, and disseminates multiple-actor, science-based knowledge on the governance of migration and integration in Sweden for societal and social sustainability. About the position As a postdoctoral researcher, you will be expected to independently and together with the other researchers contribute to: Conducting and publishing original research aligned with the Center’s thematic focus and scholarly ambition. Collaborating with fellow researchers on interdisciplinary projects Participating in the scholarly community through conferences and workshops Participating in the Center’s multistakeholder activities, e.g., workshops, roundtables, and dialogue forums Translating research findings into formats that are accessible to external audiences. Your profile The successful candidate will have built a research agenda during their PhD, as evidenced by publications, and are keen to extend methodological and theoretical expertise in the broad field of migration and integration. Their general disciplinary background should be within the social sciences, preferably with a legal, economics or business focus connected to the fields of migration and integration. The center is led by the Center Director, Associate Professor Lin Lerpold, together with the Scientific Director, Professor Laurence Romani. As a candidate, you thrive in a research environment directed towards impact, that is, a multidisciplinary and multi-paradigmatic environment where research aims at making contributions to both academic knowledge and a more sustainable society. You are open, considerate, and sympathetic to different research disciplines and paradigms such as positivist, interpretivist, and critical. You have strong qualities in both research and outreach communication activities. While successful candidates are expected to master either qualitative or quantitative  methods, knowledge of and the ability to use both are a merit. Though research aims to be published in high-ranking international journals, an interest in the Swedish context within the larger EU frame, as well as sufficient reading and oral communication in Swedish is necessary. Beyond basic academic research, the successful candidates will be expected to contribute to, and participate in, the Center’s multistakeholder activities as well as communicate their research in policy and practitioner briefs. The applicants must hold a PhD by time of employment and show an ability and ambition to publish manuscripts in highly ranked, international scholarly journals. To be eligible, applicants must have obtained their doctoral degree within the three years preceding the date of employment. This period may be extended only where special circumstances apply. Professional proficiency in English (written and spoken) is a requirement, while full proficiency in Swedish is an advantage. We expect the candidate to relocate to Stockholm. How to apply: Formal submission will be via the SSE Varbi online platform by latest October 30th, 2026. The following documents should be included in your application: A curriculum vitae A separate document listing published articles (if any) and articles submitted to journals, as well as other academic peer-reviewed publications (e.g., book chapters, conference proceedings). Copies of representative research, that is, copies of your publications or work in progress (max 5) Evidence of stakeholder engagement, for example copies or links to blogs, opinion pieces, podcasts, LinkedIn posts Names and contact information for three people willing to provide references. We recommend that you apply as soon as possible and at the latest before October 30th, 2026. Starting date is flexible but preferably around January 2027. The employment is postdoctoral employment of up to 18 month s. For further questions on the positions, please contact Lin Lerpold: lin.lerpold@hhs.se or Laurence Romani: laurence.romani@hhs.se . For HR-related questions, contact Ellen Falkenström: ellen.falkenstrom@hhs.se . About the House of Governance and Public Policy (GaPP) The SSE House of Governance and Public Policy is a multidisciplinary institution with 8 research centers housing leading researchers and educators. We conduct cutting edge research and education of societal relevance, to assist in professional development and capacity building in organizational and societal governance, and in the development of scientifically based public policy. About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment Flexible, but preferably around January 2027 Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100 City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/65 Published 25.Sep.2026 Last application date 30.Oct.2026 11:59 PM CET Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
    },
    "http://jobs.hhs.se/en/job/stockholm/tenure_track_position_at_the_department_of_accounting_stockholm_school_of_economics-970844.html": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Position",
      "description": "Tenure Track Position at the Department of Accounting, Stockholm School of Economics Available Positions Departments Back Tenure Track Position at the Department of Accounting, Stockholm School of Economics Department of Accounting The Department of Accounting at the Stockholm School of Economics invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level in accounting (including areas such as financial reporting, auditing, management accounting and control). Your profile and qualifications Qualified candidates should hold a doctoral degree and must have completed said requirement before taking up the position. As a candidate, you should have a research background in accounting, with a particular interest in digital resilience and/or risk management. You should also have an interest in conducting research that has practical implications for organizations. The successful candidate is expected to thrive in a research environment that values methodological pluralism and theoretical diversity in the study of accounting phenomena. The basic requirement is that the candidate is strong both in research and teaching. The ideal candidate is someone with a promising research record as evidenced by publications – or the credible potential to publish – in top tier accounting journals. In addition, applicants should be able to teach various accounting-related topics at the (minimum) undergraduate level. Conditions The tenure track period is 6 years, conditional on successful mid-term review after 3 years. Tenure evaluation takes place after a maximum of 6 years, and successful evaluation leads to conversion of the tenure-track position into a tenured Associate Professor position. A tentative starting date for the successful applicant is Spring 2027, but SSE is open to discussing other dates, whether earlier or later. Salaries are set on an individual basis. To be considered for the position, candidates need to submit: A letter of application articulating the candidate´s fit with the position description and profile of the department, including research interests and teaching competence, Curriculum vitae, Copies of representative research (published articles or working papers) Names and contact information of three references. The application must be received by November 14, 2026. All applications are to be sent in through the SSE recruitment system Varbi. About the department The Department of Accounting is a leading accounting department in the Nordics with about 20 faculty and 10 PhD students. Our research covers a broad range of topics related to e.g., auditing, financial accounting and reporting, management accounting & control, and sustainability accounting. Our faculty, many with an international background, regularly publish in leading accounting journals and employ both qualitative and quantitative research methods. More information about our faculty profile and research activities can be found on the SSE Department of Accounting website ( https://www.hhs.se/en/research/departments/da/people/ ). Our teaching is highly appreciated by both students and executives, and our faculty is engaged in teaching at the Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA levels as well as at SSE Executive Education. We offer a two-year Master Program in Accounting, Valuation and Financial Management, known for its practical relevance and excellent placement of the students. We also have ambitious outreach work navigated through our Accounting and Financial Management Center of Excellence (ACE) which involves corporate partners like Atlas Copco, Deloitte, Elekta, Ericsson, EY, Grant Thornton, Handelsbanken, Investor, KPMG, McKinsey, Nordea, PwC, Ratos, and Skanska. For further questions Please direct informal inquiries about the nature of the positions to one of the following: Professor Lukas Goretzki ( lukas.goretzki@hhs.se ), Head of Department Professor Kalle Kraus ( kalle.kraus@hhs.se ) For HR related queries: HR Business partner Ellen Falkenström ( ellen.falkenstrom@hhs.se ) About the Stockholm School of Economics The Stockholm School of Economics is ranked as the top business school in the Nordic and Baltic countries and enjoys a strong international reputation. World-class research forms the foundation of our educational offering, which includes Bachelor, Master, PhD, MBA, and Executive Education programs. Through creativity and collaboration, the Stockholm School of Economics provides an environment where ambitious students and accomplished researchers meet to address contemporary challenges within business and economics, particularly those concerning sustainability, diversity and innovation. Apart from delivering world class education within business and economics, SSE students are trained to be successful decision makers and leaders of the future. Our educational mission has over the years strengthened SSE students, and you can read more about it here. SSE is a member of the Stockholm Dual Career Network (SDCN) , a collaboration between universities, research institutes and companies in the Stockholm region. Through SDCN, partners of international recruits are offered professional support in establishing their careers in Sweden, including career coaching, networking opportunities, seminars and access to a broad professional network. We recognize the importance of supporting accompanying partners in international relocations and are committed to facilitating a smooth transition for the whole family. SSE is committed to a balanced gender distribution and values a variety of backgrounds and experiences among our employees. We therefore welcome all applicants regardless of their gender, ethnicity, gender identity or expression, disability, sexual orientation, age, or religion or other beliefs. We strive to have a fair and inclusive recruitment process. Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number 2026/61 Published 17.Sep.2026 Last application date 14.Nov.2026 11:59 PM CET Share links Apply for position A career page by Grade Varbi × We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here"
